<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-66) lists the Pass 3 additions and maps the 3D ECM torque, inflation and clonal Moran model to Bordeu et al. (2023), Scheele et al. (2017), Moran (1958) and Klein & Simons (2011) alongside the Pass 2 mapping to Hannezo STAR Methods; every new function carries a docstring naming its source; the math KG loop file registers equations 4-6 with `lean_locus` and `code_locus` (L94-147), and Panels G/H/I are labelled by mechanism (L1559-1633). Deductions: the PDE constants at L510 and L530-531 carry no citation or derivation comment (-4); the birth-vertex rule (L934-938) is documented as a numerical necessity but not tied to any paper statement (-2); the specimen reference values at L1917/L1927 are not marked as segmentation-derived (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L510–L531: PDE constants 0.35, 1.82, 0.55 have no citation or derivation comment <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L510-L531>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The core BARW rules (persistent migration, Poisson A -> 2A, trail deposition, R_a annihilation) are implemented in 2D (L236-489) and now in 3D (L823-1029) with the nematic alignment torque du = lambda (f.u)(f - (f.u)u) dt and a unit-sphere persistent random walk; the exact Catalan critical GW pmf (L196-234), the 1D Fisher-KPP mean field (L491-582), neutral Moran drift with hypergeometric splits (L1074-1157) and the inflating capsule (L891-903) are all recognisable reductions of the cited papers, and 6 Lean theorems machine-check the algebraic identities (0 sorry). Deductions: the 1D PDE uses uncited constants 1.82 k_a, 0.55 v_0 and v_drift = 0.35 v_0 (L510, L530-531) tuned to make the plateau hit k_b/k_a (-3); the 3D model needed a birth-vertex exemption (L934-938) absent from the 2D model, so the two simulators implement different annihilation rules (-2); the fat pad is a cylinder, not Bordeu's slab, and deposited ducts are not advected with the inflating sphere (-2); the WT 2D tree at seed 2017 has only N_b = 12 and other seeds give N_b from 1 to 70, so the 2D model sits at the edge of extinction (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L510–L531: Uncited PDE calibration constants v_drift = 0.35 v0, 1.82 ka, 0.55 v0 that set the wake plateau <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L510-L531>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
