    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1799-1998) reports 14 metrics with reference values, units and dispersion statistics: q_branch 0.480 (ref 0.5), tau = 1.4418 (ref 1.5, computed p-value L227), honest generational r = 0.924 against the measured pooled ensemble (L641-661; replaces the hand-fitted Pass 2 curve), i_inf = 0.28695 (ref 0.28571), hyper-branching 8.82x, R_a = 0 explosion +49 tips, specimen N_term = 34 and r/R_max = 0.7833, and six Pass 3 metrics: 3D cylinder q_b = 0.4937 (ref 0.5), sphere tau = 1.438 (ref 1.49), S_iso = 0.054 (ref 0), S gain 0.576, clonal f_bar = 0.119 (ref 0.125), tau_clone = 1.66 (ref 1.5). Deductions: the hyper-branching reference 2.00 (L1897) is missed by 4.4x and the \"hypo\" tree is a dead stalk (L_total = 28), yet the metric is presented as a pass (-4); i_inf vs k_b/k_a is a self-calibration via L510/L530-531 (-3); the sphere tau regresses bins with count >= 2 over S in [3, 45] of a single tree (L1824-1831) and the clone tail uses sizes 1..25 with r = -0.93 (L1198-1201) — both small-sample exponents (-3); S(lambda) monotonicity rests on one seed per lambda and the cylinder trees at lambda = 0.2, 0.4 have N_b = 4 and 2 (-2); g = 1 of the generational profile is q = 1 by construction and the reference profile is labelled \"obs\" without digitisation provenance (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L1198–L1201: Clone-size tail regression over sizes 1..25 with count >= 2; r = -0.93 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L1198-L1201>",
        "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L1824–L1831: Sphere tau regression on count >= 2 bins over S in [3, 45] of one tree (small-sample exponent) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L1824-L1831>",
        "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L1897–L1897: Hyper-branching reference 2.00 vs measured 8.82 — model/reference mismatch scored as a pass <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L1897-L1897>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-1d-mean-field-barw-homeostatic-wake-duct-density-i-inf>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-2d-barw-self-terminated-topological-branching-fraction-q-branch-wt>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-3d-barw-nematic-ecm-order-parameter-s-in-the-true-isotropic-control-chi-0-lambda-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-3d-cylindrical-fat-pad-barw-topological-branching-fraction-q-branch-ecm-lambda-0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-3d-ecm-alignment-sweep-nematic-order-gain-s-lambda-0-2-s-lambda-0-in-spherical-mesenchyme>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-3d-spherical-mesenchyme-barw-subtree-size-power-law-exponent-tau-kidney-regime>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-attenuated-tgf-beta-r-a-1-75-vs-wild-type-r-a-3-5-ductal-hyper-branching-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-clonal-neutral-drift-martingale-duct-length-weighted-labelled-fraction-vs-induced-fraction-f-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-critical-galton-watson-subtree-size-power-law-exponent-tau>,
