<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Topological Binary-Tree Balance & Critical Galton-Watson Branching Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that any finite self-terminating binary ductal tree starting from 1 primary stalk satisfies N_term = N_branch + 1, tuning the tree automatically to a critical Galton-Watson process (q_branch -> 1/2) with universal P(S) ~ S^(-3/2) subtree size scaling | Variables: N_branch: number of dichotomous tip bifurcation events (A -> 2A); N_term: number of tip-duct annihilation/termination events (A + I -> I); q_branch: ensemble branching probability" ;
    dct:source "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell 171(1):242-255 Eqs. (1)-(3); Scheele et al. (2017) Nature 542:313-317" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L115-L245>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_056_branching_random_walk_annihilation.lean#L46-L73> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def active_tips_remaining (n_branch n_term : Int) : Int := 1 + n_branch - n_term
def total_tree_segments (n_branch n_term : Int) : Int := n_branch + n_term
theorem hannezo_topological_tree_balance_and_critical_branching (n_branch : Int) :
    active_tips_remaining n_branch (n_branch + 1) = 0 ∧
    total_tree_segments n_branch (n_branch + 1) = 2 * n_branch + 1 ∧
    2 * n_branch < total_tree_segments n_branch (n_branch + 1) ∧
    active_tips_remaining 33 34 = 0 ∧
    total_tree_segments 33 34 = 67 := by
  simp [active_tips_remaining, total_tree_segments]; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "A_final = 1 + N_branch - N_term = 0  =>  N_term = N_branch + 1,  N_total = 2 N_branch + 1,  q_branch = N_branch / (N_branch + N_term) = N_branch / (2 N_branch + 1) -> 1/2 = q_term" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100033193>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature21060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39124-x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.060103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.147645> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Stochastic Branching and Annihilating Random Walk (BARW), Critical Galton-Watson Tree Topology & Fisher-KPP Travelling Wavefront" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.active_tips_remaining" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.hannezo_topological_tree_balance_and_critical_branching" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Mean-Field BARW Travelling-Wave PDE & Homeostatic Duct Density Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes that an invading pulse of active tips a(x,t) self-extinguishes behind the Fisher-KPP wavefront (a_∞ = 0) while depositing a uniform homeostatic plateau of differentiated ducts i_∞ ∝ k_b / k_a | Variables: a(x,t): active proliferative tip density; i(x,t): differentiated inactive duct density; D: tip effective diffusivity; v_0: tip speed; k_b: Poisson bifurcation rate; k_a: tip-duct annihilation kernel" ;
    dct:source "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell 171(1):242-255 STAR Methods Eqs. (4)-(10)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L250-L365>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_056_branching_random_walk_annihilation.lean#L80-L110> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def active_tip_reaction (kb ka a i : Int) : Int := kb * a - ka * a * (a + i)
def duct_deposition_rate (v0 a : Int) : Int := v0 * a
def per_tip_net_growth (kb ka a i : Int) : Int := kb - ka * (a + i)
theorem hannezo_barw_homeostatic_steady_state (kb ka v0 i_inf : Int) :
    active_tip_reaction kb ka 0 i_inf = 0 ∧
    duct_deposition_rate v0 0 = 0 ∧
    per_tip_net_growth (ka * i_inf) ka 0 i_inf = 0 := by
  simp [active_tip_reaction, duct_deposition_rate, per_tip_net_growth]; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "∂_t a = D ∇^2 a - v_0 ∇·(u_p a) + k_b a - k_a a (a + i),  ∂_t i = v_0 a;  a_∞ = 0,  i_∞ = c_0 k_b / k_a ∝ k_b / (v_0 R_a)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100033193>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature21060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39124-x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.060103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.147645> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Stochastic Branching and Annihilating Random Walk (BARW), Critical Galton-Watson Tree Topology & Fisher-KPP Travelling Wavefront" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.active_tip_reaction" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.hannezo_barw_homeostatic_steady_state" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) & Silberstein & Daniel (1987) Annihilation-Radius Hyper-Branching Density Scaling & Explosion Ablation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that attenuating TGF-beta signaling (reducing R_a) produces hyper-dense ductal trees while exogenous TGF-beta (increasing R_a) yields sparse hypoplastic trees, whereas complete ablation of annihilation (R_a = 0) destroys self-termination and triggers exponential tip explosion | Variables: R_a: tip-duct steric/TGF-beta sensing and annihilation radius; g: branching generation; N_active(g): active tip count under R_a = 0 ablation" ;
    dct:source "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell 171(1):242-255 Fig. 4; Silberstein & Daniel (1987) Science 237:291-293" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L370-L535>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_056_branching_random_walk_annihilation.lean#L117-L148> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def homeostatic_density_scaled (ra_10 : Nat) : Nat := 10000 / ra_10
def unarrested_branch_step (n : Nat) : Nat := 2 * n
def unarrested_gen5 (n : Nat) : Nat :=
  unarrested_branch_step (unarrested_branch_step (unarrested_branch_step (unarrested_branch_step (unarrested_branch_step n))))
theorem hannezo_annihilation_radius_scaling_and_explosion_ablation (n : Nat) :
    homeostatic_density_scaled 70 < homeostatic_density_scaled 35 ∧
    homeostatic_density_scaled 35 < homeostatic_density_scaled 17 ∧
    unarrested_gen5 n = 32 * n ∧ 0 < unarrested_gen5 1
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "i_∞(R_a) ∝ k_b / (v_0 R_a)  =>  i_∞(R_a,hypo) < i_∞(R_a,WT) < i_∞(R_a,hyper);  for R_a = 0 (no annihilation): N_active(g) = 2^g -> ∞" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100033193>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature21060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39124-x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.060103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.147645> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Stochastic Branching and Annihilating Random Walk (BARW), Critical Galton-Watson Tree Topology & Fisher-KPP Travelling Wavefront" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.homeostatic_density_scaled" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.hannezo_annihilation_radius_scaling_and_explosion_ablation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Anisotropic ECM Nematic Alignment Order Law for 3D BARW in cylindrical fat-pad / spherical mesenchymal geometries (Bordeu et al. 2023)" ;
    dct:description "Specifies the anisotropic-ECM torque of the 3D BARW simulator (nematic, not polar: symmetric under u -> -u, zero for isotropic matrix or perpendicular tips) and the order parameter used to quantify fiber alignment of the ductal network; S rises monotonically with lambda and over-alignment (lambda >= 0.4) collapses the tree by alignment-induced sibling annihilation | Variables: u: unit tip direction; f: ECM fiber axis; lambda: nematic alignment strength (1/time); theta: angle between a ductal segment and f; S: length-weighted nematic order parameter; gamma: capsule inflation rate" ;
    dct:source "Bordeu I, Chatzeli L, Simons BD (2023) Nat. Commun. 14:3422 (doi:10.1038/s41467-023-39124-x); Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell STAR Methods" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L801-L1066>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_056_branching_random_walk_annihilation.lean#L152-L202> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def nematic_order_twice (c : Int) : Int := 3 * c * c - 1
def nematic_torque (lambda_ fu : Int) : Int := lambda_ * fu
theorem hannezo_nematic_ecm_alignment_order (c lambda_ fu : Int) :
    nematic_order_twice 1 = 2 ∧ nematic_order_twice (-1) = 2 ∧ nematic_order_twice 0 = -1 ∧
    -1 ≤ nematic_order_twice c ∧ nematic_order_twice c = nematic_order_twice (-c) ∧
    nematic_order_twice 1 + nematic_order_twice 0 + nematic_order_twice 0 = 0 ∧
    nematic_torque 0 fu = 0 ∧ nematic_torque lambda_ 0 = 0 ∧
    nematic_torque lambda_ (-fu) = - nematic_torque lambda_ fu
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "du/dt = sigma_theta xi_perp + lambda (f.u)(f - (f.u) u);  S = < (3 cos^2 theta - 1)/2 >_length,  S(iso) = 0,  S(parallel) = 1,  S(perp) = -1/2;  R_s(t) = R_s(0)(1 + gamma t) (inflation)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100033193>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature21060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39124-x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.060103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.147645> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Stochastic Branching and Annihilating Random Walk (BARW), Critical Galton-Watson Tree Topology & Fisher-KPP Travelling Wavefront" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.nematic_order_twice" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.hannezo_nematic_ecm_alignment_order" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Scheele et al. (2017) Moran Neutral-Drift Martingale for labelled stem cells inside a terminal end bud" ;
    dct:description "Proves that neutral drift of a labelled clone inside a TEB conserves the expected labelled fraction while generating clonal variance only in mosaic TEBs; this is the reference (f_bar = f_0) against which the duct-length-weighted labelled fraction of the simulated tree is measured | Variables: N: equipotent stem cells per TEB; k: labelled cells; k': labelled cells after one Moran birth-death step" ;
    dct:source "Scheele CLGJ et al. (2017) Nature 542:313-317 (doi:10.1038/nature21060); Moran PAP (1958) Math. Proc. Camb. Phil. Soc. 54:60-71; Klein AM, Simons BD (2011) Development 138:3103-3111" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L1068-L1225>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_056_branching_random_walk_annihilation.lean#L206-L243> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def moran_expected_numerator (n k : Int) : Int :=
  (k + 1) * (k * (n - k)) + (k - 1) * (k * (n - k)) + k * (n * n - 2 * (k * (n - k)))
def moran_variance_numerator (n k : Int) : Int := 2 * (k * (n - k))
theorem scheele_moran_neutral_drift_martingale (n k : Int) :
    moran_expected_numerator n k = k * (n * n) ∧
    moran_variance_numerator n 0 = 0 ∧ moran_variance_numerator n n = 0 ∧
    (0 ≤ k → k ≤ n → 0 ≤ moran_variance_numerator n k)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P(k -> k+1) = P(k -> k-1) = k (N-k) / N^2;  E[k' | k] = k;  N^2 Var[k' - k | k] = 2 k (N-k) >= 0 (= 0 at k = 0, N)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100033193>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature21060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39124-x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.060103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.147645> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Stochastic Branching and Annihilating Random Walk (BARW), Critical Galton-Watson Tree Topology & Fisher-KPP Travelling Wavefront" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.moran_expected_numerator" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.scheele_moran_neutral_drift_martingale" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Label Conservation at a TEB Bifurcation (hypergeometric half-split + doubling)" ;
    dct:description "Shows that the A -> 2A bifurcation is label-neutral: the total labelled count doubles with cell number and each daughter is an unbiased copy of the parent, so the martingale of Law 5 extends to the whole BARW tree (clone fate is dictated by the tree's bifurcation/termination statistics, Scheele et al. 2017) | Variables: k: labelled cells in the parent TEB; k_1: labelled cells in the first half of the split; h = N/2" ;
    dct:source "Scheele CLGJ et al. (2017) Nature 542:313-317 (doi:10.1038/nature21060)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L1088-L1157>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_056_branching_random_walk_annihilation.lean#L247-L272> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def daughter_labels (k k1 : Int) : Int × Int := (2 * k1, 2 * (k - k1))
theorem scheele_teb_split_label_conservation (k k1 h : Int) :
    (daughter_labels k k1).1 + (daughter_labels k k1).2 = 2 * k ∧
    2 * (h * k) = (2 * h) * k
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "k -> (2 k_1, 2 (k - k_1)),  k_1 ~ Hypergeom(N, k, N/2);  2 k_1 + 2 (k - k_1) = 2 k;  E[2 k_1] = k" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100033193>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature21060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39124-x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.060103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.147645> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Stochastic Branching and Annihilating Random Walk (BARW), Critical Galton-Watson Tree Topology & Fisher-KPP Travelling Wavefront" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.daughter_labels" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_056.scheele_teb_split_label_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

